AI Task Prompt — Migrate to Firebase Authentication + Firestore profiles

Goal: Replace the current custom/login-with-Firestore approach and use Firebase Authentication for sign-up/sign-in (email/password). Keep all profile data and app data in Firestore under Users/{uid}. Do not store passwords in Firestore.

Instructions for the agent:

Environment: repo root contains the web app. Use client web SDK (Firebase v9 modular) for auth and Firestore. Use Firebase Admin SDK (Cloud Functions or a trusted script) for any migration or setting custom claims.
Config: expect the operator to provide Firebase config (API key, projectId, etc.) before running.
Required changes (high-level)

Client:
Replace current register/login handlers with Firebase Auth calls.
On successful signup, create a Firestore document at Users/{uid} with profile fields (firstname/lastname/company/payplan/…); do NOT write password.
On sign-in, read Users/{uid} and populate existing local state/localStorage as the app expects.
Use onAuthStateChanged to drive UI (show/hide protected nav pages) instead of relying solely on localStorage.isLoggedIn.
Firestore:
Update firestore.rules to require request.auth != null for profile reads/writes and allow admin access using custom claims.
Admin:
Provide a migration script (Node.js Admin SDK) or Cloud Function to create Firebase Auth accounts for existing Firestore users and trigger password-reset emails OR to import users securely.
