Suggested secure Firestore rules (concise example to add/replace in firestore.rules):

Ensure Users/{userId} readable/writable only by owner or admin:
match /Users/{userId} {
allow create: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
allow read, update, delete: if request.auth != null && (request.auth.uid == userId || request.auth.token.admin == true);
match /chats/{chatId} {
allow read, write: if request.auth != null && (request.auth.uid == userId || request.auth.token.admin == true);
}
}
Use request.auth.token.admin for admin checks (set with Admin SDK).
Migration options (pick one)

Option A (recommended): Admin script creates Auth accounts for existing emails with random passwords, then call sendPasswordResetEmail for each user so users set their own password.
Option B (advanced): If you can verify hashes server-side with the exact original hashing scheme, import users using Auth import with hash params.
Option C: Force re-registration (less ideal for UX).
